# Active ignores (container image built FROM the published @squadrules/mcp npm package):
# CVE-2026-12151 (undici WebSocket DoS): npm-bundled undici in the Node.js base image at
# /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/undici. The app's own undici is pinned to a
# patched version by the Dockerfile `overrides`. Not exploitable in production (npm is not
# used at runtime). Fix requires a Node.js base image digest update.
# Added: 2026-07-06, review by: 2026-10-06
CVE-2026-12151

# CVE-2026-93748 (http-cache-semantics information disclosure): the runtime image installs
# the published package with `npm install --omit=dev`, so no dev-only release tooling
# (semantic-release -> @semantic-release/npm -> npm -> make-fetch-happen ->
# http-cache-semantics) is present. The only remaining source is npm's OWN bundled copy in
# the Node base image (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/http-cache-semantics).
# It is never imported by server runtime code and npm is not used at runtime, so it is not
# exploitable in production. No upstream fix exists (4.2.0 is the latest published version),
# so it cannot be remediated by upgrade or npm override. Revisit when upstream ships a patch
# or the Node base image bundles a fixed npm.
# Added: 2026-10-03, review by: 2027-01-03
CVE-2026-93748

# Resolved:
# CVE-2026-45447 (OpenSSL Heap Use-After-Free in PKCS7_verify) resolved:
# node:24-alpine digest updated to include OpenSSL 3.5.7-r0.
